  "passages": {
    "en": [
      {
        "pointer": "/sections/0/blocks/0",
        "anchor": "article-body",
        "text": "Civilizational structures eventually enter daily life through air, housing, transport, work, income and living costs. Living environment shapes basic conditions, employment connects people to resources and career paths, and the margin between income and necessary costs affects household buffers and capacity to change."
      },
      {
        "pointer": "/sections/0/blocks/1",
        "anchor": "article-body",
        "text": "Macroeconomic growth and lived experience are not interchangeable. Under similar employment rates or average incomes, stability, accessible opportunity and necessary costs can still differ substantially."
      },
      {
        "pointer": "/sections/0/blocks/2",
        "anchor": "article-body",
        "text": "This article remains within the completed Book VI manuscript; B6-WEB-B does not add live current-data population. Subjective experience and structural conditions remain distinct, and no single measure is used to infer a person or an entire society."
      }
    ],
    "zh-Hans": [
      {
        "pointer": "/sections/0/blocks/0",
        "anchor": "article-body",
        "text": "文明结构最终会进入空气、住房、交通、工作、收入与生活成本。生活环境决定日常基础条件，就业把个人接入社会资源与职业路径，收入与必要成本之间的余量则影响家庭缓冲和转换能力。"
      },
      {
        "pointer": "/sections/0/blocks/1",
        "anchor": "article-body",
        "text": "宏观增长与个人体验不能自动画等号。相同就业率或平均收入之下，稳定性、可进入机会与必要成本仍可能非常不同。"
      },
      {
        "pointer": "/sections/0/blocks/2",
        "anchor": "article-body",
        "text": "本文以第六册已完成书稿为边界；B6-WEB-B 不补充实时当前数据。主观体验与结构条件分开观察，不从单一指标推断个人或整个社会。"
      }
    ]
  },
